AO6SJc6Ycgxp","user":{"login":"yosoyfreeman","id":64601424,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY0NjAxNDI0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/64601424?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/yosoyfreeman","html_url":"https://github.com/yosoyfreeman","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yosoyfreeman/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yosoyfreeman/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yosoyfreeman/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yosoyfreeman/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yosoyfreeman/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yosoyfreeman/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yosoyfreeman/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yosoyfreeman/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yosoyfreeman/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-12-20T19:35:01Z","updated_at":"2024-12-20T19:35:01Z","body":"Hi! I seen the proposal, but it contains some gameplay specific choices like walk/run, modifying the velocity when changing direction for game feel purposes etc.  As it's clear on the discussion, such things can be really specific and are hard to implement in a generic way. This proposal is meant to keep the same functionality we already have, just solving the input, acceleration and up direction issues. I also tried to make more clear how to properly handle acceleration along the horizontal plane and gravity-jump along the up direction.\r\n\r\nSo this proposal is more about fixing what we have and polishing it than it is about offering more features.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2557611113/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2557614951","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/100662#issuecomment-2557614951","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/100662","id":2557614951,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6Ychtn","user":{"login":"AThousandShips","id":96648715,"node_id":"U_kgDOBcK-Cw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/96648715?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips","html_url":"https://github.com/AThousandShips","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-12-20T19:37:27Z","updated_at":"2024-12-20T19:37:27Z","body":"That's a PR with code changes to the same templates so good to get the context from those discussions ","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2557614951/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2557618782","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/100662#issuecomment-2557618782","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/100662","id":2557618782,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6Ycipe","user":{"login":"yosoyfreeman","id":64601424,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY0NjAxNDI0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/64601424?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/yosoyfreeman","html_url":"https://github.com/yosoyfreeman","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yosoyfreeman/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yosoyfreeman/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yosoyfreeman/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yosoyfreeman/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yosoyfreeman/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yosoyfreeman/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yosoyfreeman/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yosoyfreeman/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yosoyfreeman/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-12-20T19:40:44Z","updated_at":"2024-12-20T19:40:44Z","body":"Thank you a lot for the review! I'll try to have it fixing as soon as possible!\r\n\r\nPS: Yes i think the linked PR is relevant! I was just trying to add context to what this one aims for exactly.\r\n\r\nThank you a lot again! ","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2557618782/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":1,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2557639367","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/100662#issuecomment-2557639367","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/100662","id":2557639367,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6YcnrH","user":{"login":"yosoyfreeman","id":64601424,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY0NjAxNDI0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/64601424?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/yosoyfreeman","html_url":"https://github.com/yosoyfreeman","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yosoyfreeman/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yosoyfreeman/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yosoyfreeman/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yosoyfreeman/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yosoyfreeman/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yosoyfreeman/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yosoyfreeman/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yosoyfreeman/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yosoyfreeman/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-12-20T19:57:48Z","updated_at":"2024-12-20T19:57:48Z","body":"I fixed the issues, i think everything is correct now. If that's not the case, tell me and i'll work on it. Thank you!","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2557639367/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2558191298","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/100662#issuecomment-2558191298","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/100662","id":2558191298,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6YeubC","user":{"login":"Gertkeno","id":15616419,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE1NjE2NDE5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/15616419?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Gertkeno","html_url":"https://github.com/Gertkeno","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Gertkeno/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Gertkeno/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Gertkeno/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Gertkeno/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Gertkeno/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Gertkeno/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Gertkeno/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Gertkeno/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Gertkeno/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-12-21T18:08:03Z","updated_at":"2024-12-22T19:45:59Z","body":"Really good fixes to the template. I think it's a great starting point now that it's corrected key issues.\r\n\r\nKnockback has been challenging for new developers to make with the preivous templates, I see that as a common forum help post; this template very directly fixes those issues, allowing physics driven forces to affect the character bodies.\r\n\r\nA lot of developers would slot animations into the if/else direction: and that remains easy to do, though not as obvious. Luckily any old tutorial using the last template should hint at that implementation.\r\n\r\nMany do not even notice the old template does not support controllers despite how close it was, just removing `.normalized()` helps.\r\n\r\n\r\nI am glad nothing else is added, this template should focus on legiblity and being extensible! I could see myself explaining this to a 10 year old easily, skipping over orthonormalized as _rotates the input_ haha.","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2558191298/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":1,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2558296438","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/100662#issuecomment-2558296438","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/100662","id":2558296438,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6YfIF2","user":{"login":"yosoyfreeman","id":64601424,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY0NjAxNDI0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/64601424?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/yosoyfreeman","html_url":"https://github.com/yosoyfreeman","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yosoyfreeman/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yosoyfreeman/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yosoyfreeman/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yosoyfreeman/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yosoyfreeman/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yosoyfreeman/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yosoyfreeman/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yosoyfreeman/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yosoyfreeman/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-12-22T01:52:47Z","updated_at":"2024-12-22T01:52:47Z","body":"I just noticed that we are calling jump_velocity to a variable that represents the jump_speed, as speed is just a scalar (what the variable actually is) and velocity implies a vector, which is misleading for the user.\r\n\r\nAlso, i understand the intention of using constant for the parameters, but things as the speed, the acceleration and the jump speed should be exposed to the editor as i see it.  It would also show the user how to export variables.\r\n\r\nWhat do you think? i personally think that exporting them makes more sense, more having into account that constants in gdscript can be changed anyway.\r\n\r\nHearing your thoughts.\r\n\r\nThank you!","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2558296438/reactions","total_count":3,"+1":3,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2561064203","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/100662#issuecomment-2561064203","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/100662","id":2561064203,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6Ypr0L","user":{"login":"yosoyfreeman","id":64601424,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY0NjAxNDI0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/64601424?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/yosoyfreeman","html_url":"https://github.com/yosoyfreeman","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yosoyfreeman/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yosoyfreeman/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yosoyfreeman/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yosoyfreeman/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yosoyfreeman/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yosoyfreeman/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yosoyfreeman/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yosoyfreeman/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yosoyfreeman/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-12-24T12:19:33Z","updated_at":"2024-12-24T12:20:51Z","body":"Ok, i pushed the latest changes and i think everything should be right!\r\n\r\nThis is the final work involved in this PR:\r\n\r\n- Fixed the input distortion issue.\r\n- support for controllers.\r\n- Implemented a correct way to accelerate without square root distortion due each axis using the max acceleration.\r\n- Implemented a variable for acceleration instead of using the max speed.\r\n- Fixed FPS dependency on the acceleration. This is a non trivial issue, but with the current code it's easy to visualize work with. As long as the acceleration is not wrongly manipulated by the user by using some kind of multiplier, we should be OK.\r\n\r\n- General refractor of the code.\r\n\r\n- Fixes some consistency errors with typed vars.\r\n\r\n- Change jump_velocity to jump_speed to reflect that is indeed a scalar, not a vector.\r\n\r\n- Exposes speed, accceleration and jump speed to the editor, showing the user how to do it and the correct annotation for both gdscript and c#\r\n\r\nI think that's it. I personally like the result a lot and got good feedback, but of course, feel free to tell me if you think it needs further corrections.\r\n","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2561064203/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":2,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]